story += [p('3.4.4 Data Flow Description', 'Sub'), p('During registration, user details move from the React form to the Express authentication route. The backend validates the fields, hashes the password, and persists the User document. During login, credentials are checked against the stored hash. A JWT cookie is then sent to the browser. For protected operations, the browser includes the cookie, authentication middleware validates it, and the relevant controller performs the requested action.', 'Body'), p('For real-time communication, the backend creates a Stream token after verifying the EchoChat user. The frontend uses that token to connect directly to Stream services. For AI requests, the frontend sends the question to the backend; the backend communicates with Gemini, so the Gemini key remains protected.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]
story += [p('3.5 Functional Requirements', 'Main'), grid([['ID','Requirement'],['FR-01','The system shall allow registration with name, email, and password.'],['FR-02','The system shall authenticate valid credentials and issue a protected session.'],['FR-03','The system shall allow profile onboarding with language preferences.'],['FR-04','The system shall recommend eligible non-friend users.'],['FR-05','The system shall create and accept friend requests.'],['FR-06','The system shall issue Stream tokens only for authenticated users.'],['FR-07','The system shall support real-time one-to-one chat and video calls.'],['FR-08','The system shall support AI queries, translation, and language detection.'],['FR-09','The system shall persist visual theme preference in browser storage.']], [.85*inch,5.65*inch]), p('Table 3.6: Functional Requirements', 'Caption'), p('3.6 Non-Functional Requirements', 'Main')] + bullets(['Security: passwords are hashed with bcrypt; JWT routes are protected; service secrets are held in environment variables.', 'Usability: responsive user interface, page loading feedback, accessible forms, and meaningful error messages.', 'Performance: TanStack Query avoids unnecessary repeated server requests; Stream manages real-time synchronization.', 'Maintainability: separate routes, controllers, middleware, models, and reusable frontend components.', 'Reliability: server errors return appropriate HTTP status codes without exposing sensitive data.']) + [PageBreak()]

# Chapter 4 pages 13-19
story += [p('CHAPTER 4', 'CoverTitle'), p('IMPLEMENTATION AND TESTING', 'CoverTitle'), p('4.1 Database Design', 'Main'), p('MongoDB is used because the application has user profiles with optional fields and relationship references. Mongoose defines the User and FriendRequest schemas. The User model includes identity, profile, language, onboarding, and friend-list information. The FriendRequest model records the sender, recipient, status, and timestamps.', 'Body')]
story += diagram('Figure 4.1: Database Relationship Diagram', ['User: _id, fullName, email, password, profile details', 'FriendRequest: sender, recipient, status', 'Accepted Request Updates Both User Friend Lists'])
story += [p('4.1.1 User Collection', 'Sub'), grid([['Field','Description'],['_id','Unique MongoDB object identifier.'],['fullName','Name shown in the user profile.'],['email','Unique login email address.'],['password','bcrypt hashed password; never returned in normal user responses.'],['bio, profilePic, location','Optional profile information.'],['nativeLanguage, learningLanguage','Language-exchange preferences.'],['isOnboarded','Controls access to social features.'],['friends','References to other User documents.']], [2.15*inch,4.35*inch]), p('Table 4.1: User Collection Fields', 'Caption'), PageBreak()]
story += [p('4.1.2 FriendRequest Collection', 'Sub'), grid([['Field','Description'],['_id','Unique MongoDB object identifier.'],['sender','Reference to the User who sends the request.'],['recipient','Reference to the User who receives the request.'],['status','Current status: pending or accepted.'],['createdAt, updatedAt','Automatic timestamps maintained by Mongoose.']], [2.15*inch,4.35*inch]), p('Table 4.2: FriendRequest Collection Fields', 'Caption'), p('4.2 Module / Class Diagram', 'Main'), p('Although JavaScript uses modules rather than traditional classes for every feature, the backend is organized into clear responsibility units. AuthController handles registration, login, logout, and current-user retrieval. UserController handles onboarding, recommendations, friend requests, and request acceptance. ChatController generates Stream tokens. AIController communicates with Gemini. User and FriendRequest Mongoose models encapsulate persistent data.', 'Body')]
story += diagram('Figure 4.2: Backend Module Structure', ['Routes', 'Authentication Middleware', 'Controllers', 'User and FriendRequest Models', 'MongoDB / Stream / Gemini Services'])
story += [p('4.3 Frontend Implementation', 'Main'), p('The React frontend uses pages and reusable components. React Router manages client-side navigation. Axios sends credentialed requests to the backend. TanStack Query manages asynchronous server data such as the current user, recommendations, and friend requests. Zustand stores the selected theme and local storage preserves it across browser sessions.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]
story += [p('4.4 Backend Implementation', 'Main'), p('The Express backend exposes separate route groups for authentication, users, chat, and AI. Authentication middleware reads the JWT cookie and verifies the user before protected actions. Controllers return JSON responses and meaningful status codes. Mongoose executes database operations, while Stream and Gemini calls are initiated only from backend code.', 'Body'), grid([['Route Group','Example Responsibilities'],['/api/auth','Sign up, login, logout, retrieve authenticated user.'],['/api/users','Onboarding, recommended users, friend requests, request acceptance.'],['/api/chat','Generate authenticated Stream user token.'],['/api/ai','AI chat, text translation, and language detection.']], [1.5*inch,5.0*inch]), p('Table 4.3: Major API Route Groups', 'Caption'), p('4.5 Testing Approach', 'Main'), p('The project was tested through manual functional testing, API testing with Postman, form validation checks, and end-to-end user-flow verification in the browser. The purpose of testing was to verify both successful actions and invalid-input responses. Authentication, onboarding, friend requests, protected access, and AI endpoints were checked with expected and incorrect inputs.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]
test_rows=[['Test ID','Feature','Input / Condition','Expected Result','Status'],['TC-01','Registration','Valid name, email, password','Account is created; password is hashed; session is issued.','Pass'],['TC-02','Registration','Existing email address','System returns duplicate-email error.','Pass'],['TC-03','Login','Valid email and password','JWT cookie is created; user reaches onboarding or home.','Pass'],['TC-04','Login','Incorrect password','System returns invalid-credential error.','Pass'],['TC-05','Onboarding','All required fields provided','Profile saves and isOnboarded becomes true.','Pass'],['TC-06','Friend request','Request sent to another eligible user','Pending request is created.','Pass'],['TC-07','Friend request','Request sent to self or duplicate request','System rejects the request.','Pass'],['TC-08','Chat token','Authenticated user requests token','Backend returns valid Stream token.','Pass'],['TC-09','AI request','Authenticated user submits text','Gemini response is returned through backend.','Pass'],['TC-10','Protected route','No valid JWT cookie','System denies access and returns authentication error.','Pass']]
story += [p('4.6 Test Cases', 'Main'), grid(test_rows,[.65*inch,1.0*inch,1.75*inch,2.55*inch,.55*inch]), p('Table 4.4: Functional Test Cases', 'Caption'), p('4.7 Test Result Summary', 'Main'), p('The test cases show that the core workflow operates correctly: a user can create an account, authenticate, complete a profile, discover users, manage a friend request, obtain a secure Stream token, and use the AI endpoint. Error paths return clear responses for duplicate registration, invalid login, unauthorized access, and invalid friend-request actions.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]
story += [p('4.8 Demonstration Flow', 'Main'), p('The application demonstration begins with account registration and secure login. The user then completes onboarding by entering language preferences. The home screen displays recommended learners. After a friend request is accepted, the user opens a one-to-one chat. The chat interface uses an authenticated Stream connection and may share a video-call link. Finally, the AI assistant is opened to submit a language question, request translation, or detect a language.', 'Body')]
story += diagram('Figure 4.3: Implementation and Demonstration Flow', ['Register', 'Login', 'Complete Profile', 'Find Language Partners', 'Friend Request', 'Real-Time Chat', 'Video Call', 'Gemini AI Assistance'])
story += [p('4.9 Security Considerations', 'Main')] + bullets(['Passwords are hashed with bcrypt before storage.', 'JWT cookies protect authenticated sessions and private APIs.', 'Backend middleware verifies the user before protected actions.', 'MongoDB, JWT, Stream, and Gemini secrets are stored in environment variables.', 'Stream user tokens are generated by the backend rather than the browser.']) + [PageBreak()]
story += [p('4.10 Limitations of Current Implementation', 'Main'), p('The current version is focused on one-to-one interaction and depends on active internet connectivity and third-party service availability. The recommendation process uses available profile and friendship information; it does not yet use advanced matching scores. A formal language-level test, persistent AI conversation history, group chats, notification delivery, moderation, user blocking, and full automated test coverage are planned improvements.', 'Body'), p('4.11 Deployment Readiness', 'Main'), p('For production deployment, the frontend and backend should be hosted using HTTPS. The production frontend origin must be allowed through CORS. Secure cookies must be enabled in production. All secrets must be added through the hosting provider environment settings rather than committed to source control. MongoDB access must be restricted using secure credentials and allowed network access.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]

# Chapter 5 pages 20-21
story += [p('CHAPTER 5', 'CoverTitle'), p('CONCLUSION', 'CoverTitle'), p('5.1 Conclusion', 'Main'), p('AI Powered EchoChat Application demonstrates a practical integration of modern web development, real-time communication, and generative AI for a language-exchange use case. The project provides a secure workflow in which a learner can register, complete a language profile, discover users, form a connection, communicate through chat and video, and obtain AI support without moving between unrelated applications.', 'Body'), p('The project strengthened understanding of React component design, REST API development with Express, MongoDB schema modeling, JWT authentication, password hashing, state management, server-state handling, and third-party API integration. It also showed the importance of keeping service credentials on the backend and separating route, controller, middleware, and model responsibilities.', 'Body'), p('5.2 Achievements', 'Main')] + bullets(['Implemented secure authentication with bcrypt and JWT cookies.', 'Designed onboarding and profile data for language-exchange use.', 'Implemented user discovery and friend-request lifecycle.', 'Integrated Stream services for chat and video calling.', 'Integrated Gemini AI through protected backend APIs.', 'Created a responsive React interface with theme persistence.']) + [PageBreak()]
story += [p('5.3 Future Enhancements', 'Main')] + bullets(['Language-based compatibility score and personalized partner recommendations.', 'Group chat rooms and group video sessions for practice communities.', 'Language-level test, score tracking, and learning plans.', 'Persistent AI chat history and richer structured AI feedback.', 'Push notifications for friend requests and messages.', 'User blocking, reporting, moderation, rate limiting, and audit logs.', 'Automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests.', 'Analytics dashboard for learning activity and feature usage.']) + [p('5.4 Final Remarks', 'Main'), p('The application can be extended incrementally because its client-server structure, database models, controllers, and external integrations are organized by responsibility. EchoChat therefore provides a solid foundation for a broader language-learning community platform.', 'Body'), PageBreak()]

